IMPORT prelude

-- Accounting Standards Act 2007 (Singapore) -- who the Committee's accounting standards may reach (s 8(1)), when a standard has
-- force (ss 9(3), 10(2)), the Committee's size, quorum, presiding member and delegation (ss 4, 5, 7), the definition of
-- "statutory body" (s 2), and which statutory bodies must follow the Accountant-General's standards (s 12 and the Schedule).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ASA2007.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 17 of 2026 (in force 1 July 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. An institutional Act with no offences and no
-- penalties: SCOPED to the provisions with decision content. Not encoded: the objects the Committee must pursue (s 9(1), (2)) beyond
-- their effect on validity, the evidence rules (s 10(3)), the Accountant-General's choice of text (s 11(2), (3)), terms of office
-- and revocation of appointments (s 4(5)-(7), (9)), the transitional carry-over of Accounting Standards Council standards
-- (s 8(4), (5)), and the Minister's power to amend the Schedule and make rules (ss 13, 14). The content of any accounting standard
-- is not in the Act and is not encoded.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Accounting Standards Act 2007 -- standards and statutory bodies`

§§ `8(1) -- who the Committee's standards may reach`

-- s 3: the Authority makes accounting standards "applicable to companies for the purpose of the Companies Act 1967" and "to any
-- other entities specified in section 8(1)".
-- s 8(1): standards "may be expressed to apply" to (a) companies; (b) co-operative societies registered under the Co-operative
-- Societies Act 1979; (c) societies registered under the Societies Act 1966; (d) charities registered, and institutions of a public
-- character approved or deemed approved, under the Charities Act 1994 -- in each case all of them or specified classes.
-- The last three entries below are not named in s 8(1); that they fall outside it is a reading of the list, not a statement in the
-- text. Statutory bodies have their own standards under Part 4.
DECLARE Entity IS ONE OF
    `a company`
    `a registered co-operative society`
    `a registered society`
    `a registered charity`
    `an institution of a public character`
    `a statutory body`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `a sole proprietorship`

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` IF
    CONSIDER `the entity`
    WHEN `a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered co-operative society` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered society` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered charity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an institution of a public character` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `9(3) and 10(2) -- when a Committee standard has force`

-- s 10(1): the Committee "must" publish a notice of the making of a standard, stating its date, the entities it covers and where
-- it may be inspected.
-- s 10(2): "No accounting standard, no amendment to the accounting standard and no revocation of the accounting standard has any
-- force or effect ... until the notice relating thereto is published in accordance with subsection (1)."
-- s 9(3): "A failure to comply with this Part in relation to the making or formulation of an accounting standard does not affect the
-- validity of the standard." So a standard made without regard to the s 9 objects is still valid; but it has no force until notice.
-- s 10 is itself in Part 3. How s 9(3) and s 10(2) meet when the notice is defective is not resolved here; this encoding follows
-- s 10(2) and treats an unpublished notice as no force.
GIVEN `made by the Committee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notice of making published` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the s 9 objects were observed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notice of revocation published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the standard has force` IF
        `made by the Committee`
    AND `notice of making published`
    AND (NOT `notice of revocation published`)

§§ `4 -- the Committee's membership`

-- s 4(2): the Committee consists of "(a) the Chairperson; (b) at least 10 but not more than 15 other members."
GIVEN `has a Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee is composed as s 4(2) requires` IF
        `has a Chairperson`
    AND `number of other members` >= 10
    AND `number of other members` <= 15

-- s 4(1): the Authority appoints "with the approval of the Minister". s 4(3): "A person must not be appointed ... unless the
-- person's knowledge of, or experience in, business, accounting, law or government or other relevant fields qualifies the person".
GIVEN `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `qualified by knowledge or experience` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be appointed a member` IF
    `the Minister approved` AND `qualified by knowledge or experience`

-- s 4(8): a member "may resign ... at any time by giving at least one month's notice in writing to the Authority."
GIVEN `notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `given to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resignation notice complies` IF
        `notice in writing`
    AND `given to the Authority`
    AND `months of notice` >= 1

§§ `5 -- meetings`

-- s 5(2): "one half of the number of its members constitutes a quorum." Read here (an inference) as: present members are at least
-- half the members, i.e. twice those present is not less than the total. With 11 members, 6 are needed.
GIVEN `members of the Committee` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` * 2 >= `members of the Committee`

-- s 5(3): "The Chairperson presides at all meetings ... but if the Chairperson is absent -- (a) the temporary Chairperson; or
-- (b) if there is no temporary Chairperson, the member that the members present elect".
-- That the temporary Chairperson must also be present to preside is an inference.
DECLARE Presider IS ONE OF
    `the Chairperson`
    `the temporary Chairperson`
    `a member elected by those present`

GIVEN `the Chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN, `a temporary Chairperson is appointed and present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Presider
DECIDE `who presides` IS
    IF `the Chairperson is present`
    THEN `the Chairperson`
    ELSE IF `a temporary Chairperson is appointed and present`
         THEN `the temporary Chairperson`
         ELSE `a member elected by those present`

§§ `7 -- sub-committees and delegation`

-- s 7(2): "The chairperson of every sub-committee ... must be a member of the Committee." (3): a sub-committee "may include persons
-- who are not members of the Committee."
GIVEN `is a member of the Committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may chair a sub-committee` IF `is a member of the Committee`

GIVEN `is a member of the Committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sit on a sub-committee` IF TRUE

-- s 7(4): the Committee may delegate "(a) to any of its members; or (b) to any sub-committee appointed by it ... any of the functions
-- or powers of the Committee under this Act, except the power of delegation conferred by this section."
-- (6): the Committee may continue to exercise a delegated power.
-- The other powers listed are drawn from ss 7(1), 8(3) and 6(2); treating them as delegable is a reading of "any ... except".
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `making accounting standards`
    `issuing practice directions`
    `appointing sub-committees`
    `the power of delegation`

DECLARE Delegate IS ONE OF
    `a member of the Committee`
    `a sub-committee appointed by the Committee`
    `a person who is not a member`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the delegate` IS A Delegate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee may delegate` IF
        (NOT (`the power` EQUALS `the power of delegation`))
    AND (NOT (`the delegate` EQUALS `a person who is not a member`))

§§ `2 -- statutory body`

-- s 2: "statutory body" means a body "(a) established or constituted by or under a public Act; (b) that has a public function; and
-- (c) whose annual report and audited financial statements are required by written law to be presented to Parliament."
GIVEN `established under a public Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a public function` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `accounts must be presented to Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a statutory body` IF
        `established under a public Act`
    AND `has a public function`
    AND `accounts must be presented to Parliament`

§§ `11(4), 12 and the Schedule -- who must follow the Accountant-General's standards`

-- s 12: "The accounts and financial statements of every statutory body specified in the Schedule must be prepared in compliance with
-- the accounting standards that are established under this Part and notified in writing to the statutory body by the
-- Accountant-General." s 11(4): a standard "applies to any periods specified in the standard".
-- A sample of bodies. Those marked IN appear in the deposited Schedule (items 6, 19, 21, 3, 8A, 59); the last two do not appear in
-- it. Whether those two are "statutory bodies" under s 2 is not decided here. Items 5 and 63 are deleted and their former
-- occupants are not named in the deposit.
DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `the Central Provident Fund Board`
    `the Housing and Development Board`
    `the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore`
    `the Board of Architects`
    `the Communicable Diseases Agency`
    `the Skills and Workforce Development Agency`
    `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    `the Public Service Commission`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is listed in the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `the Monetary Authority of Singapore` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Public Service Commission` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body,
      `established by the Accountant-General under Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notified in writing to the body` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the period is one the standard specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body must prepare its accounts in compliance with the standard` IF
        `is listed in the Schedule` `the body`
    AND `established by the Accountant-General under Part 4`
    AND `notified in writing to the body`
    AND `the period is one the standard specifies`
